# Ruijie RGOS `show manuinfo` parser (Phase 49-D-11).
#
# Sample input (templates/samples/ruijie_10_62_63_23_show_manuinfo.txt):
#   Device 1
#     Location: Chassis
#     Device name: System
#     Device Serial Number: G1M913U000351
#     ...
#   Device 2
#     Location: Slot-1
#     Device Serial Number: G1P7293000128
#     ...
#
# Field semantics:
#   DEVICE_ID         — Ruijie internal device index (1 = chassis, 2..N = slots)
#   LOCATION          — chassis (Location: Chassis) or Slot-N (Location: Slot-1 ...)
#   DEVICE_NAME       — module model string for slot rows; "System" for chassis
#   SN                — vendor-issued serial number for this physical entity
#
# Strategy: emit ONE record per physical entity (chassis or slot). The
# project's homegrown textfsm parser (internal/templates/textfsm.go)
# applies strings.TrimSpace to each line BEFORE rule matching, so the
# rule patterns should NOT use leading \s+ — they must match against
# already-trimmed text. Each Device block ends with a "Mac Address:"
# line; we attach `-> Record` there to flush the previous block before
# the next `Device N` line overwrites DEVICE_ID.

Value DEVICE_ID (\d+)
Value LOCATION (\S.*?)
Value DEVICE_NAME (\S.*?)
Value SN (\S.*?)
Value HARDWARE_VERSION (\S.*?)
Value SOFTWARE_VERSION (\S.*?)
Value MAC_ADDR (\S.*?)

Start
  ^Device\s+${DEVICE_ID}\s*$$
  ^Location:\s+${LOCATION}\s*$$
  ^Device\s+name:\s+${DEVICE_NAME}\s*$$
  ^Device\s+Serial\s+Number:\s+${SN}\s*$$
  ^Hardware\s+Version:\s+${HARDWARE_VERSION}\s*$$
  ^Software\s+Version:\s+${SOFTWARE_VERSION}\s*$$
  ^Mac\s+Address:\s+${MAC_ADDR}\s*$$ -> Record